course: dictionary
lesson: 2869
title: Don: part of don't, an old verb and a name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Don» is often only part of a longer word. In texts you will mostly meet it as the start of «don't», as in «Don't run near the pool». The apostrophe shows that letters are missing. Read the whole word: don't means do not.
explain: «Don» can also be an old-fashioned verb in stories. «The knight donned his armour» means the knight put his armour on. Donned is the past tense, and donning means putting on. Today we say put on or wear, so you will mostly find this word in older books.
explain: Don is also a name, short for Donald. A don is a teacher at Oxford or Cambridge University. In «a blend of the Squire and the College Don», the squire is a country landowner and the don is a university teacher. The words around the word tell you which meaning is right.
fact: «Don» is usually a fragment of «don't», which means «do not».
fact: To «don» clothes means to put them on, and «donned» is the past tense.
fact: «Don» is a man's name, short for Donald.
fact: A «don» is a university teacher, especially at Oxford or Cambridge.
fact: Use the context to decide: is it part of «don't», an old verb, a name or a teacher?
exercise: «Don't run near the pool.» What does don't mean here? | done and dusted | do now | *do not | does not matter
exercise: «The knight donned his armour.» What does donned mean? | sold | took off | *put on | lost
exercise: Don is a man's name. What is it short for? | Daniel | Dennis | *Donald | Dominic
test: In «the College Don», what is a don? | *a university teacher | a country landowner | a knight in armour | a kind of pool
test: Which word is the past tense of don, meaning to put on clothes? | don't | dons | donning | *donned
exam: Which meaning fits «Don't climb the wall»? | a name | a teacher | *a shortened form of do not | to put on clothes
